    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.SNuXttNqxzJ6uPXv]{Caitiff} who grew up on Milwaukee's streets and ran with the Zulu Nation street gang until it collapsed, Turk was Embraced in 1975 by Gengis, an Anarch of standing in Chicago, then promptly abandoned. Rather than dying off like most weak-blooded @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.SNuXttNqxzJ6uPXv]{Caitiff}, Turk clawed his way into leadership of the East Side Anarchs Union &mdash; the second largest Anarch gang in Milwaukee &mdash; and has committed diablerie at least once to strengthen his blood. He commands the eastern half of Downtown from a derelict riverboat in Veterans Park, waging a losing turf war against Akawa's @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.antitribu.JournalEntry.hs33xrNXWT2UXXS4]{Blood Brothers}. Unknown to Turk, the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.ZJx9H3XnU8yQGy9s]{Malkavian} Esau has been quietly Dominating him for years, feeding his paranoia that all the Kindred of Milwaukee are plotting against him.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Dark, sombre, and bitter. The pain of your life has made you distrustful of everyone. You genuinely believe the whole city is out to destroy you and the Union.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Gengis (an Anarch of standing in Chicago, largely absent). Haven: a broken-down riverboat in Veterans Park (Union base). Disciplines as printed: Celerity 2, Dominate 2, Fortitude 2, Potence 1 (capped above to this system's 1-5 scale). Secretly manipulated by the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.ZJx9H3XnU8yQGy9s]{Malkavian} Jacob/Esau.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
